	(text "I got this so far is this correct do you think?\n\nIFOUT — Analog Out. 480 MHz IF output from the mixer/IF front-end; normally routed out to an external SAW band-pass filter and back into IFIN. \nopendevices.ru\n\nIFIN — Analog In. Return from the SAW filter into the chip’s IF amplifier/demod chain. Keep the IFOUT–SAW–IFIN path very short/controlled. \nopendevices.ru\n\nBBOUT2 — Analog Out. FM video baseband (demod) buffer output. Typically AC-coupled and fed to the internal video amp input (VAMPIN), with optional external RC shaping. \nopendevices.ru\n\nVAMPIN — Analog In. Video amplifier input (takes the demodulated video from BBOUT2). \nopendevices.ru\n\nVAMPOUT — Analog Out. Video amplifier output; drive your CVBS output here (AC-couple and terminate for ~1 Vpp into 75 Ω). \nopendevices.ru\n\nFMIN_65 — Analog In. 6.5 MHz audio subcarrier input to the audio demod path; normally taken from the video baseband via a 6.5 MHz ceramic band-pass filter placed between FMIN_65 and AUIN_65. \nopendevices.ru\n+1\n\nAUIN_65 — Analog In. Input to the 6.5 MHz audio demod/amp after the ceramic filter. \nopendevices.ru\n\nAUOUT_65 — Analog Out. Demodulated audio output from the 6.5 MHz path (line-level; AC-couple). \nopendevices.ru\n\nVT_65 — Analog Out. 6.5 MHz audio demodulator VCO/PLL loop node (“audio demod out” in table). You add the small RC loop-filter network here; community docs show a working network (e.g., ~200 Ω/430 k/470 pF/100 pF + 4.7 µF). \nopendevices.ru\n+1\n\nAGC_C — Analog I/O. AGC rectifier/output node for the IF chain; decouple with a capacitor to set AGC dynamics. You can also monitor it as an AGC indicator. (For a calibrated strength output, use RSSI pin IFPDC_C.)\n\n\nOthers input is also appreciated!!!\nImage\nImage\nCVBS → ADV7180/ADV7280/TVP5150 (BT.656) →\n\nSTM32F7/H7 (DCMI + LTDC) → RGB TFT, or\n\nESP32-S3 (parallel in + RGB LCD) for modest resolutions, or\n\nRaspberry Pi (Zero 2/4) via USB AV capture → HDMI/DSI.\n\nAudio: RTC6715 AFOUT → I²S codec/ADC → SoC, or bypass SoC and go straight to an amp.\n\n\nAnd for dealing with audio and video, what should be best? i was thinking a class D amp for audio but for the video processing so i can output on a common oled or tft lcd not sure?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 729.996 617.982 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7691e7b6-4d2c-4fdc-a207-e114f6d76d3f")
	)
