	(text "Awesome—let’s lock it in for AT043TN24 V.4 (backlight = 9 LEDs in series, 28.8 V typ / 31.5 V max @ 20 mA).\n\nTPS61169 setup (values you can place)\n\nVIN (to TPS61169): 3.3 V (your schematic’s 3.3V_A rail).\n\nI_LED (backlight current): 20 mA → RSET = 0.204 V / 0.02 A = 10.2 Ω (FB→GND).\n\nInductor (L): 4.7 µH, Isat ≥ 1 A (good margin; e.g., Coilcraft LPS4018-472ML, Isat≈1.9 A).\n\nSchottky diode (D): Use ≥ 60 V reverse rating (e.g., SS16 / MBR0560).\nWhy 60 V? Your string is ~29–31.5 V and the IC’s open-LED protection can push VOUT toward ~37–39 V; 60 V gives safe headroom (40 V parts like SS14 are marginal here).\n\nInput cap (CIN): 4.7 µF, ≥ 6.3 V X5R/X7R, close to VIN/GND pins.\n\nOutput cap (COUT): 2.2–4.7 µF, ≥ 50 V X5R/X7R, close to LED+ return node. (50 V covers 31.5 V max plus spikes.)\n\nCTRL (PWM dimming): Drive from your AMT630A B/L_EN/PWM pin (5–100 kHz).\n\nLayout: Keep SW–L–D–COUT loop short and fat; place CIN tight to VIN/GND; put RSET right at FB.\n\nWhat voltages/currents you’ll see\n\nVOUT (LED+): Set by LED string → ≈ 28.8 V typ, ≈ 31.5 V max (TPS61169 can go up to ~38–39 V with OVP).\n\nI_LED (through backlight): 20 mA (fixed by RSET=10.2 Ω).\n\nIIN (from 3.3 V): ≈ 0.21 A at 28.8 V/20 mA (assuming ~85% efficiency).\nCalculation: \n𝐼\n𝐼\n𝑁\n≈\n𝑉\n𝑂\n𝑈\n𝑇\n⋅\n𝐼\n𝐿\n𝐸\n𝐷\n𝜂\n⋅\n𝑉\n𝐼\n𝑁\n⇒\n28.8\n⋅\n0.02\n0.85\n⋅\n3.3\n≈\n0.205\n \nA\nI\nIN\n	​\n\n≈\nη⋅V\nIN\n	​\n\nV\nOUT\n	​\n\n⋅I\nLED\n	​\n\n	​\n\n⇒\n0.85⋅3.3\n28.8⋅0.02\n	​\n\n≈0.205 A. (Budget 200–220 mA.)\n\nSwitch/inductor peak current (check): with L=4.7 µH, f≈1.2 MHz, worst case near OVP, ≈ 0.55 A peak—well below the TPS61169 min 1.2 A current limit and fine for a ≥1 A-Isat inductor.\n\nHook-up (matches your schematic)\n\nSW → inductor → VIN, Schottky from SW/inductor node to LED+; LED− → FB → RSET → GND; CTRL from B/L_EN. (Exactly the same block where your KA2708 sat.)\n\nIf you want, share the exact panel datasheet page for the LED spec it lists; I’ll sanity-check the RSET, finalize COUT voltage, and suggest specific Mouser part numbers for L/D/C that drop straight in."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
